{
  "description": "One shared table for the address a link destination arrives at.\n\nA destination is delivered to readers with different dialects, and each writes it in the spelling its own surface can hold. Two spellings are not evidence that they name one page, so this file asserts the relationship instead of listing two strings: tests/test_link_unit_delivery.py renders `markdown` through the real Slack adapter and asserts the address it decodes out of the wrapper is `address`, and ui/src/components/ui/markdown.test.tsx renders the same `markdown` through the real Markdown component and asserts the browser URL parser resolves that anchor's href and `address` to the same URL. Neither side can drift without the other failing.\n\nNavigation equivalence is all this table claims. The exact bytes each surface puts on its own wire are asserted separately, beside the adapter that writes them.",
